# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>

# --- COMMIT END ---
# Type can be:
#  build    (changes that affect the build system or external dependencies)
#  chore    (routine maintenance that does not change production behavior)
#  ci       (changes to CI configuration files and scripts)
#  docs     (changes to documentation)
#  feat     (new user-facing feature)
#  fix      (fix addressing a user bug)
#  perf     (performance-related change)
#  refactor (refactoring production code)
#  revert   (reversion in code)
#  style    (formatting changes - no production code logic changes)
#  test     (adding or refactoring tests - no production code changes)
#
# Scope is optional and names a granular context for the changes.
#
# Common scopes for this project:
# cli, config, deps, docs, engine, model, release, targets, util
#
# Subject: imperative mood, say what you did.
# Body: go into detail about the changes.
# Footer: related or resolved GitHub issue keys.
#
# Example:
#   feat(engine): add hooks feature support for kiro-ide
#
#   Implemented pre- and post-tool-use hook generation for the
#   kiro-ide target, mapping the canonical hooks.jsonc format to
#   the .kiro/agents/default.json hooks array.
#
#   Closes #42
